b.com/eslint/eslint","homepage":"https://eslint.org","size":51012,"stargazers_count":26698,"watchers_count":26698,"language":"JavaScript","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":4866,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":103,"license":{"key":"mit","name":"MIT License","spdx_id":"MIT","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/mit","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTEz"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["ecmascript","eslint","javascript","linter","static-code-analysis"],"visibility":"public","forks":4866,"open_issues":103,"watchers":26698,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"I was using Karma the other day and became enamored with its `init` command. Basically, running `karma init` walks you through a questionnaire that helps create an initial configuration file. The more I thought about it, the more I think we need something like that for ESLint in 1.0.0.\n\nSo here's what I'm thinking:\n\n```\n$ eslint --init\n```\n\nThis will _not_ do any linting, but rather will start up a questionnaire about the user's settings. It needs to be short enough that people will want to do it, but long enough so the most important pieces are set. Here's what I think should be in the questions:\n1. What style of indentation do you use? Tabs or Spaces\n   - If spaces, how many spaces?\n2. What quotes do you use for strings? Double or Single\n3. What line endings do you use? Windows or Unix\n4. Do you require semicolons? Yes or No\n5. Which of these libraries are you using? React, Angular\n   - If any are chosen, automatically install `eslint-plugin-react` or `eslint-plugin-angular` based on selection.\n6. Are you using ECMAScript 6 features? Yes or No\n   - If yes, enable `es6` environment.\n7. Where will your code run? Browser, Node.js\n   - Set appropriate environment\n8. What format do you want your config file to be in? JSON or YAML\n\nWe can use https://github.com/SBoudrias/Inquirer.js to make this easy, and once complete, output a `.eslintrc` file with these filled in.\n\nThis would probably be implemented as a new object (let's say, `Initializer`?).\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/2302/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/2302/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":336275259,"node_id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDMzNjI3NTI1OQ==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/events/336275259","actor":{"login":"btmills","id":1709537,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MDk1Mzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1709537?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills","html_url":"https://github.com/btmills","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"labeled","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2015-06-21T21:35:28Z","label":{"name":"bug","color":"fc2929"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"id":336275260,"node_id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDMzNjI3NTI2MA==","url":"https://api.github.com/r